  "question": {
    "text": "The resistance of a wire at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. At which temperature, its resistance will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>?</mo></math>",
    "image": null
